{"name":"Camelot","hex":"#803a4b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Camelot","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A mythical location in England and the stronghold of King Arthur in the Arthurian legend.","The administration and surrounding mystique of President John F. Kennedy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Camelot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Camelot","blocks":[{"text":"Camelot is a legendary castle and court associated with King Arthur. Absent in the early Arthurian material, Camelot first appeared in 12th-century French romances and eventually came to be described as the fantastic capital of Arthur's realm and a symbol of the Arthurian world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Idylls_of_the_King_3.jpg/330px-Idylls_of_the_King_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camelot","wikidata":"Q220437"},{"title":"Camelot (musical)","blocks":[{"text":"Camelot is a musical with music by Frederick Loewe and lyrics and a book by Alan Jay Lerner. It is based on the legend of King Arthur as adapted from the 1958 novel The Once and Future King by T. H. White."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f6/Camelot_Original_Cast_Recording.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camelot_(musical)","wikidata":"Q1028491"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Siedl%C4%99cin_Wie%C5%BCa_Ksi%C4%85%C5%BC%C4%99ca_Gotyckie_malowid%C5%82a_%C5%9Bcienne_Zamek_Camelot_i_Kr%C3%B3lowa_Ginewra.JPG/500px-Siedl%C4%99cin_Wie%C5%BCa_Ksi%C4%85%C5%BC%C4%99ca_Gotyckie_malowid%C5%82a_%C5%9Bcienne_Zamek_Camelot_i_Kr%C3%B3lowa_Ginewra.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Siedl%C4%99cin_Wie%C5%BCa_Ksi%C4%85%C5%BC%C4%99ca_G